# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored and must never be committed.

# The only external credential Propositum needs.
# Get one at https://console.anthropic.com -> API keys.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Local SQLite file. Not a secret — a path. Relative paths resolve from prisma/.
DATABASE_URL="file:../propositum.db"

# The unpacked extension's id, from chrome://extensions after Load unpacked.
# Without it the app rejects every capture request with `bad-origin` — the
# response says so, rather than failing silently.
#
# OPTIONAL SINCE 2026-08-26, and left here because setting it still works and
# still wins. `/welcome` pairs the extension from a screen: it lists the ids
# that have knocked in the last five minutes, and one click writes a row. No
# restart — `resolveExtensionOrigin` in src/server/extension-pairing.ts reads
# this variable first and the row second, so a clone that pins an id behaves
# exactly as it did before that page existed and is never quietly overridden by
# a click.
#
# Leave it blank and nothing is loosened. An install with no answer refuses
# everything, which is the state a fresh clone is in and the state /welcome
# exists to get somebody out of.
PROPOSITUM_EXTENSION_ID=

# ── Google Calendar free/busy (ADR-0014). Entirely optional. ─────────────────
#
# THE APP'S OWN credentials, which is why they are here and the per-person
# refresh token is not: these identify Propositum, they are the same for every
# copy built from this source, and they say nothing about anybody. The refresh
# token identifies the PERSON, so it lives in their SQLite file where they can
# delete it.
#
# Leave these blank and the feature is ABSENT — not broken, not an error. No
# screen mentions a calendar, nothing is read, and no request leaves the machine.
#
# ONE EXCEPTION, added 2026-08-18 and deliberate: if you connected a calendar and
# THEN blanked these, the front door still shows that connection with a
# Disconnect beside it. Blanking a variable does not delete a credential — your
# refresh token is a row in your SQLite file — and a stored credential the
# product will not show you is one you cannot remove. Disconnect first, or
# disconnect after; either works, and neither needs these values.
#
# To fill them in: Google Cloud Console -> APIs & Services -> Credentials ->
# Create credentials -> OAuth client ID -> Desktop app, then add
# http://127.0.0.1:3117/api/calendar/callback as an authorised redirect URI.
# The only scope Propositum ever asks for is
# https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.freebusy — "View your availability in
# your calendars", which returns start/end times and no titles.
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Where the loopback redirect comes back to. Only set this if `npm run dev` is
# on a port other than 3117.
# PROPOSITUM_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3117

# ── The phone thread (ADR-0021). Entirely optional, and NOT set here. ────────
#
# There is deliberately no TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN variable. The bot is one you make
# yourself through @BotFather, it identifies YOU rather than the application,
# and it is therefore a per-person credential — so it lives in your SQLite file
# where you can delete it, next to the calendar refresh token and for the same
# reason. Pair it on /welcome; unpair it there too.
#
# Leave it unpaired and the feature is ABSENT: no screen speaks, nothing is
# sent, and no request leaves the machine. What it sends when paired is derived
# prose about your own work — what Propositum thinks you are on, why it
# stopped, what it needs decided. Those sentences sit on Telegram's servers and
# are not encrypted end to end. ADR-0021 opens on that price rather than
# burying it.
